      <section class="section wrap" id="features">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">LESS SETUP. MORE EXPRESSION.</p><h2>Everything you need.<br />Room for your own ideas.</h2><p>A familiar workflow for developers. A thoughtful reading experience for everyone.</p></div>
        <div class="features">
          <article><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">M↓</span><h3>Just write Markdown.</h3><p>Your posts are plain text files. Add a title, write your story, and let OpenBlog take care of the page.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><h3>Your content. Your repository.</h3><p>Keep every word and every revision in git. Move your site whenever you want, with your history intact.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">◐</span><h3>Feels like your space.</h3><p>Light and dark themes, your own colors, and your own identity. A single config file brings it together.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><h3>Small footprint. Open web.</h3><p>Astro builds a static site. Publish on GitHub Pages or your favorite static host, with no database to maintain.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">⊞</span><h3>A home for every topic.</h3><p>Folders become categories. Tags connect ideas. Featured posts and an archive help readers find their next read.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">&lt;/&gt;</span><h3>Open from the first line.</h3><p>MIT licensed and ready to make your own. Read the source, change the details, or contribute something back.</p></article>
        </div>
